Design a KiCad PCB for the following:
Create a 4 layer esp32 board with a temperature sensor and a rgb led. It should be powered and programmed by USB-C
Follow the repository's AGENTS.md instructions and use the ee-design skill to drive the design process.
Start from the intended function, develop a sensible architecture, select and verify suitable components, then create and review the schematic before proceeding to PCB placement and routing.
Use reasonable engineering judgment and research where needed. Make sensible assumptions rather than asking me about every unspecified detail. Only ask me if a missing decision would materially change what the product is supposed to be.
Create and maintain the normal design/ state/documentation for the project as defined by the skill.
Continue through the design workflow as far as the available tools and validation allow. Do not skip engineering review just because ERC or DRC passes.